  "headline": {
    "id": "google-wyoming-investment-and-power-plan-20261108",
    "date": "2026-11-08",
    "title": "Google’s $17B Wyoming data-center plan includes 702MW fuel-cell development",
    "summary": "Google’s November 5 announcement sets out a long-term $17 billion investment for its first Wyoming data center. Its power plan includes a 702MW Bloom fuel-cell development through AEP. That arrangement is older evidence: AEP’s October 14 release describes a 20-year power purchase agreement and targets full operation of the generating facility by the end of 2028. This is generation capacity, not data-center IT power or proof of commissioned compute. Carbon capture is planned, while a separate Tallgrass turbine retrofit remains under engineering study. Google does not provide a data-center opening date or an annual spending schedule for the $17 billion.",
